{
  "sn47.14:0.1": "Linked Discourses 47.14 ",
  "sn47.14:0.2": "2. At Nāḷandā ",
  "sn47.14:0.3": "At Ukkacelā ",
  "sn47.14:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Vajjis near Ukkacelā on the bank of the Ganges River, together with a large Saṅgha of mendicants. It was not long after Sāriputta and Moggallāna had become fully quenched. ",
  "sn47.14:1.2": "Now, at that time the Buddha was sitting in the open, surrounded by the Saṅgha of mendicants. ",
  "sn47.14:2.1": "Then the Buddha looked around the Saṅgha of mendicants, who were silent. He addressed them: ",
  "sn47.14:2.2": "“Mendicants, this assembly seems empty to me now that Sāriputta and Moggallāna have become fully quenched. ",
  "sn47.14:2.3": "My assembly never used to be empty; I had no concern for any region where Sāriputta and Moggallāna stayed. ",
  "sn47.14:2.4": "The Buddhas of the past or the future have pairs of chief disciples who at best were like ",
  "sn47.14:2.5": "Sāriputta and Moggallāna were to me. ",
  "sn47.14:2.6": "",
  "sn47.14:2.7": "It’s an incredible and amazing quality of such disciples ",
  "sn47.14:2.8": "that they fulfill the Teacher’s instructions and follow his advice. And they’re liked and approved, respected and admired by the four assemblies. ",
  "sn47.14:2.9": "And it’s an incredible and amazing quality of the Realized One ",
  "sn47.14:2.10": "that when such a pair of disciples becomes fully quenched he does not sorrow or lament. ",
  "sn47.14:2.11": "How could it